1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Prooflane — Proof Before Payment.
A CSV can look valid and still contain the wrong records.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Live Gemini drafts measurable checks from the brief.
The client sets the price. AI cannot approve work or payment.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Review all seven requirements and attach the original source.
Agree explicitly. CSV rows stay local.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:48,000
This delivery substitutes an order.
The five structural checks pass; source reconciliation fails.

5
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The total still matches: 285.
Missing and unexpected source keys block approval and checkout.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Now change revenue by just one cent.
Decimal comparison detects the exact -0.01 difference.

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Review the proposed correction against the agreed source.
No invented data, generated code or silent file changes.

8
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Apply is explicit. Undo restores the previous preview.
Both require fresh verification before approval.

9
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:52,000
All seven checks pass on the corrected version.
Explicit approval freezes the agreement, source, price and delivery hash.

10
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Checkout is now eligible for this approved delivery.
The following receipt is from a SEPARATE verified sandbox run.

11
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Separate run: actual USD 1.00 PayPal sandbox capture.
The same seven-check workflow; a distinct project and transaction.

12
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Export its evidence and verify the original files separately.
The verifier does not need the original project database.

13
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Authenticated, read-only PayPal lookup confirms this capture,
exact USD amount and version 2 manifest reference.

14
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:45,000
A changed delivery fails verification.
Prooflane connects reviewed work, approval and checkout. github.com/AaryaMody1301/Prooflane
